      "text": "### Blocking IFN Induction"
    },
    {
      "id": "05-IMMUNE-EVASION.md#007",
      "path": [
        "05-IMMUNE-EVASION.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
        "backsource_ids": "[mdloom-backfill:virology:05-immune-evasion, git-history:virology:05-immune-evasion]",
        "canonical_path": "virology/05-IMMUNE-EVASION.md",
        "concepts": "[immune, evasion]",
        "current_path": "virology/05-IMMUNE-EVASION.md",
        "id": "maxim:virology:immune-evasion",
        "index_roles": "[guide, root-concept]",
        "kind": "guide",
        "maxim_schema": "maxim.frontmatter.v1",
        "module": "virology",
        "remap_from": "[]",
        "remap_to": "[]",
        "root_concepts": "[immune, evasion]",
        "section": "virology",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Immune Evasion Strategies",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "**Influenza NS1:**\n```\n  NS1 (non-structural protein 1, 26 kDa) is the major innate antagonist of influenza."
    },
    {
      "id": "05-IMMUNE-EVASION.md#008",
      "path": [
        "05-IMMUNE-EVASION.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
        "backsource_ids": "[mdloom-backfill:virology:05-immune-evasion, git-history:virology:05-immune-evasion]",
        "canonical_path": "virology/05-IMMUNE-EVASION.md",
        "concepts": "[immune, evasion]",
        "current_path": "virology/05-IMMUNE-EVASION.md",
        "id": "maxim:virology:immune-evasion",
        "index_roles": "[guide, root-concept]",
        "kind": "guide",
        "maxim_schema": "maxim.frontmatter.v1",
        "module": "virology",
        "remap_from": "[]",
        "remap_to": "[]",
        "root_concepts": "[immune, evasion]",
        "section": "virology",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Immune Evasion Strategies",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "Mechanisms:\n  1. RNA binding: NS1 sequesters dsRNA, preventing RIG-I and PKR activation\n  2. TRIM25 inhibition: TRIM25 ubiquitinates RIG-I for activation; NS1 binds\n     TRIM25 and blocks RIG-I ubiquitination → no IFN signaling\n  3. CPSF30 binding: NS1 blocks host mRNA 3'-processing → prevents ISG mRNA\n     from being polyadenylated and exported (host cell shutoff)\n  4. PI3K activation: NS1 activates PI3K → Akt → prevents premature apoptosis"
    },
    {
      "id": "05-IMMUNE-EVASION.md#009",
      "path": [
        "05-IMMUNE-EVASION.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
        "backsource_ids": "[mdloom-backfill:virology:05-immune-evasion, git-history:virology:05-immune-evasion]",
        "canonical_path": "virology/05-IMMUNE-EVASION.md",
        "concepts": "[immune, evasion]",
        "current_path": "virology/05-IMMUNE-EVASION.md",
        "id": "maxim:virology:immune-evasion",
        "index_roles": "[guide, root-concept]",
        "kind": "guide",
        "maxim_schema": "maxim.frontmatter.v1",
        "module": "virology",
        "remap_from": "[]",
        "remap_to": "[]",
        "root_concepts": "[immune, evasion]",
        "section": "virology",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Immune Evasion Strategies",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "Pandemic strains often have NS1 mutations affecting effector binding:\n  1918 pandemic H1N1 NS1: highly effective IFN antagonist\n  Avian H5N1 NS1: hyperinduces cytokines (overcomes IFN block paradoxically)\n```"
    },
    {
      "id": "05-IMMUNE-EVASION.md#010",
      "path": [
        "05-IMMUNE-EVASION.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
        "backsource_ids": "[mdloom-backfill:virology:05-immune-evasion, git-history:virology:05-immune-evasion]",
        "canonical_path": "virology/05-IMMUNE-EVASION.md",
        "concepts": "[immune, evasion]",
        "current_path": "virology/05-IMMUNE-EVASION.md",
        "id": "maxim:virology:immune-evasion",
        "index_roles": "[guide, root-concept]",
        "kind": "guide",
        "maxim_schema": "maxim.frontmatter.v1",
        "module": "virology",
        "remap_from": "[]",
        "remap_to": "[]",
        "root_concepts": "[immune, evasion]",
        "section": "virology",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Immune Evasion Strategies",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "**SARS-CoV-2 and coronaviruses:**\n```\n  Multiple evasion mechanisms:\n  nsp3 (PLpro): deubiquitinase activity strips ISG15/ubiquitin from\n                signaling proteins → blocks IFN signaling\n  nsp14 ExoN:   removes dsRNA markers → less RIG-I/MDA5 activation\n  nsp15 EndoU:  cleaves viral dsRNA within DMVs before it escapes\n  nsp1:         binds ribosome; blocks host mRNA translation\n  ORF6:         blocks nuclear import by binding KPNA2 (importin-α)\n  ORF3b, ORF9c: additional IFN pathway inhibitors\n  DMV formation: sequesters dsRNA from cytoplasmic sensors\n```"
    },
    {
      "id": "05-IMMUNE-EVASION.md#011",
      "path": [
        "05-IMMUNE-EVASION.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
        "backsource_ids": "[mdloom-backfill:virology:05-immune-evasion, git-history:virology:05-immune-evasion]",
