        "root_concepts": "[immune, evasion]",
        "section": "virology",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Immune Evasion Strategies",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "Even after IFN is produced, viruses block JAK-STAT signaling:"
    },
    {
      "id": "05-IMMUNE-EVASION.md#013",
      "path": [
        "05-IMMUNE-EVASION.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
        "backsource_ids": "[mdloom-backfill:virology:05-immune-evasion, git-history:virology:05-immune-evasion]",
        "canonical_path": "virology/05-IMMUNE-EVASION.md",
        "concepts": "[immune, evasion]",
        "current_path": "virology/05-IMMUNE-EVASION.md",
        "id": "maxim:virology:immune-evasion",
        "index_roles": "[guide, root-concept]",
        "kind": "guide",
        "maxim_schema": "maxim.frontmatter.v1",
        "module": "virology",
        "remap_from": "[]",
        "remap_to": "[]",
        "root_concepts": "[immune, evasion]",
        "section": "virology",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Immune Evasion Strategies",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "```\n  Paramyxoviruses (V protein):\n  Mumps V binds STAT1 and STAT2 → prevents phosphorylation\n  PIV2 V: targets STAT2 for proteasomal degradation\n  Simian virus 5: degrades STAT1\n  Nipah V: nuclear STAT sequestration"
    },
    {
      "id": "05-IMMUNE-EVASION.md#014",
      "path": [
        "05-IMMUNE-EVASION.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
        "backsource_ids": "[mdloom-backfill:virology:05-immune-evasion, git-history:virology:05-immune-evasion]",
        "canonical_path": "virology/05-IMMUNE-EVASION.md",
        "concepts": "[immune, evasion]",
        "current_path": "virology/05-IMMUNE-EVASION.md",
        "id": "maxim:virology:immune-evasion",
        "index_roles": "[guide, root-concept]",
        "kind": "guide",
        "maxim_schema": "maxim.frontmatter.v1",
        "module": "virology",
        "remap_from": "[]",
        "remap_to": "[]",
        "root_concepts": "[immune, evasion]",
        "section": "virology",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Immune Evasion Strategies",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "Adenovirus:\n  E1A: binds histone deacetylase complexes → represses ISG promoters\n  VA RNA I: decoy dsRNA → saturates PKR without activating it"
    },
    {
      "id": "05-IMMUNE-EVASION.md#015",
      "path": [
        "05-IMMUNE-EVASION.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
        "backsource_ids": "[mdloom-backfill:virology:05-immune-evasion, git-history:virology:05-immune-evasion]",
        "canonical_path": "virology/05-IMMUNE-EVASION.md",
        "concepts": "[immune, evasion]",
        "current_path": "virology/05-IMMUNE-EVASION.md",
        "id": "maxim:virology:immune-evasion",
        "index_roles": "[guide, root-concept]",
        "kind": "guide",
        "maxim_schema": "maxim.frontmatter.v1",
        "module": "virology",
        "remap_from": "[]",
        "remap_to": "[]",
        "root_concepts": "[immune, evasion]",
        "section": "virology",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Immune Evasion Strategies",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "Result: even if IFN is made, the JAK-STAT cascade is blocked in\n  virus-infected cells (autocrine protection) and sometimes neighboring cells\n```"
    },
